hadiths[496]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mughira ibn Muslim - a truthful Muslim - narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of this hadith, except that he said: Then he began narrating to us that Gog and Magog are from the children of Adam, and that if they were released upon people they would ruin their livelihoods; none of them dies without leaving a thousand or more of his offspring; and beyond them are three nations: Tawil, Taris, and Mansak."
"2402","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Abd Allah ibn Babah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and the ten days were mentioned in his presence - and he said: There are no days in which deeds are more beloved to Allah, mighty and majestic, than the ten of Dhu al-Hijja. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the path of Allah? He deemed it great and said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except a man who goes out with himself and his wealth and stakes his very life in it."
"2403","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, saying: A man of Banu al-Harith narrated to me, saying: A man of ours called Ayyub narrated to me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amr say: Whoever repents a year before his death, it is accepted of him; whoever repents a day before his death, it is accepted of him; whoever repents an hour before his death, it is accepted of him. I said to him: But Allah, mighty and majestic, says: {Repentance with Allah is only for those who do evil in ignorance}, the verse. He said: I only narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2404","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Isa ibn Talha, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Sacrifice while upon his mount, with people asking him; a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not think stoning came before sacrifice, so I sacrificed before stoning. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stone, and no harm. Another began saying: O Messenger of Allah, I did not realize shaving came before sacrifice, so I sacrificed before shaving. He said: Shave, and no harm. He said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked that day about what a person forgets or does not know of putting rites before one another, and the like, but he said: Do that, and no harm."
"2405","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not dispute about the Quran, for disputing about it is disbelief."
"2406","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Muhammad ibn Sirin and Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Hanafi, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in an enclosure of the enclosures of Madinah when a man sought permission. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. It was Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, so I permitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he drew near praising Allah until he sat. Then a loud-voiced man sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. It was Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, so I permitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and he drew near praising Allah. Then a soft-voiced man sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Permit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise despite a tribulation that will befall him. So I permitted him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise; it was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, and he drew near praising Allah until he sat. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Where am I? He said: You are with your father."
"2407","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Fayyad, saying: I heard Abu Iyad narrating from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fast one day of the month and you have the reward of the rest; fast two days and you have the reward of the rest; fast three days and you have the reward of the rest."
"2408","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from Abu Yahya al-A'raj, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing."
"2409","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from Abu Yahya al-A'raj, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon people performing ablution - while on a journey - and said: Perfect the ablution; woe to the heels from the Fire - or: to the ankles; Shu'ba doubted which."
"2410","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Rabi'a ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi, from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Amr: It reached me that you narrate that the wretched is one wretched in his mother's womb. He said: I do not permit anyone to lie about me; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, created His creation in darkness, then cast upon them light from His light; whoever it touched was guided, and whoever it missed went astray."
"2411","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, who said: I testify that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, does not lift knowledge by snatching it away, but lifts scholars with their knowledge, until when no scholar remains, people take ignorant leaders; they are asked and narrate, so they go astray and lead astray."
"2412","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Abd Allah ibn Amr came to Nawf and said: Narrate, for we have been forbidden from narration. He said: I would not narrate while a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Quraysh is present. Abd Allah ibn Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be an emigration after an emigration; the best of the earth will go out to the emigration-place of Ibrahim, peace be upon him, while the worst of its people remain on earth; their lands expel them, the Self of Allah loathes them, and the Fire gathers them with apes and pigs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will emerge from the east reciting the Quran without it passing their throats; every time a horn is cut off a horn grows, every time a horn is cut off a horn grows, every time a horn is cut off a horn grows; then among their remainder emerges the Dajjal."
"2413","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard a man of Banu Makhzum narrating from his uncle, that Mu'awiya wanted to take al-Waht from Abd Allah ibn Amr, so he ordered his retainers to arm themselves. He was reproached for that, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"2414","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Mansur informed me, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Shumayt ibn Nubayt, from Jaban, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: None enters Paradise who is undutiful to parents, nor a reminder of favors, nor a child of adultery, nor an addict."
"2415","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir four times over al-Najashi."
"2416","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you say on Friday to your brother while the imam preaches: Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk."
"2417","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, walk with tranquillity upon you; pray what you catch and make up what you miss."
"2418","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, that a man of Banu Fazara cried out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, my wife bore me a black boy; how is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there any dusky one among them? He said: Yes. He said: How is that? He said: A strain drew it, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this too may be a strain that drew him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not permit him to disown him."
"2419","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The fitra is five: trimming nails, shaving the pubes, plucking the armpit, the siwak, and circumcision."
"2420","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not outbid one another, let no townsman sell for a Bedouin, let no man propose over the proposal of his brother, nor sell over his sale."
"2421","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him, will soon descend among you as a just judge; he will kill the pig, break the cross, abolish the jizya, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"2422","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of a Muslim upon his brother is five: returning greeting, visiting the sick, following the funeral, accepting the invitation, and blessing the sneezer."
"2423","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fara' and no atira. Sa'id said: The fara' is the first offspring produced which they used to slaughter for their idols, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them from it; the atira is the sacrifice of Mudar in Rajab, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them from it."
"2424","With the same chain, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said: Your brother al-Najashi has died, so stand and pray over him. He said: He rose and we rose with him until he reached al-Baqi'; he went forward and arranged us behind him, and said takbir over him four times."
"2425","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayra, that two women of Hudhayl - one threw a stone at the other and killed her and what was in her womb - so they disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who assigned for her fetus a ghurra, a slave or slave-girl, decreed the blood-money of the woman upon her kin, and gave her and her child and those with them inheritance. Then Ibn al-Nabigha al-Hudhali came and said: O Messenger of Allah, must one pay for one who neither ate nor drank, nor spoke nor cried out? Should the like of that be void?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is of the brethren of soothsayers, on account of the rhymed speech he uttered."
"2426","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intense heat is from the blast of Hell, so cool the prayer."
"2427","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id or another, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast, to which the rich are invited and the poor left out; whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"2428","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No three children of a Muslim die without the Fire touching him except to fulfil the oath. Al-Zuhri said: As though he meant this verse: {There is none of you but will come to it}, the verse."
"2429","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dumb beast - its wound is without liability, the mine is without liability, the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"2430","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured, count thirty."
"2431","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: I narrated to Abu Ishaq, from Ma'mar ibn Rashid and Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra - Shu'ba said: One of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fara' and no atira. And the other said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the fara' and the atira."
"2432","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has cursed the Jews - or: Allah has fought the Jews - fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their price."
"2433","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Hassan, answer on behalf of the Messenger of Allah; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit."
"2434","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, the freedman of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral in the mosque gets nothing. Salih said: I met men among those who met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr; when they came and found no place but to pray in the mosque, they returned and did not pray."
"2435","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people sit in a gathering in which they do not remember Allah and send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but it is a cause of regret upon them."
"2436","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage: This is the only one, then staying upon the mats. He said: They all used to travel except Zaynab and Sawda, for they said: No mount shall move us after what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2437","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was broad in the forearms, wide between the shoulders, with long eyelashes; he was not loud in the markets, nor obscene nor deliberately obscene; he turned wholly and turned away wholly."
"2438","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him bathe; whoever carries a bier, let him perform ablution."
"2439","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic, loves sneezing and dislikes yawning; when one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah, and it is a duty upon whoever hears him to say: May Allah have mercy on you. When he yawns, Satan laughs, so let him suppress it as much as he can."
"2440","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O believing women, let no neighbor belittle her neighbor even with a sheep's trotter."
"2441","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, saying: Sa'id narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a day except with a mahram."
"2442","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The seven oft-repeated verses are the Opening of the Book."
"2443","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'as then gave salutation. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It was neither shortened nor did I forget. The people said: Indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned and prayed two rak'as, then prostrated two prostrations."
"2444","With the same chain, he said: Abu Hurayra said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from bowing he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise. He said takbir between the two prostrations, and when he rose and when he lowered."
"2445","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has with him a wrong against his brother - of honor or wealth - let him discharge it to him before there comes to him the Day of Resurrection in which neither dinar nor dirham is accepted; if he has righteous deeds, they are taken from him and given to its owner, and if he has no righteous deeds, the sins of its owner are taken and loaded upon him."
"2446","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you is saved by his deeds. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him. Be upright and draw near - or: come near - set out in the evening and morning, take a portion of the night journey, aim for moderation, aim for moderation, and you will reach."
"2447","With the same chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never sated, and a supplication that is not heard."
"2448","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the women and children in houses, I would order one to call the prayer - meaning the last Isha prayer - then burn down upon people who stay behind from prayer - meaning the last Isha prayer - in their houses."
"2449","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of women is she whom, when you look at her, she pleases you; when you command her, she obeys you; when you are absent from her, she guards you in herself and your wealth. He said: And he recited this verse: {Men are guardians over women}, to the end of the verse."
"2450","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: There is no prophet but warned his community of the Dajjal - or he said: cautioned his community of the Dajjal. I shall say among you what no prophet before me said: He is one-eyed, and your Lord, blessed and exalted, is not so; written between his eyes is: disbeliever."
"2451","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Umari narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a man between whom and his brother is a wrong of honor or wealth, who discharges it to him before there comes upon him a day in which neither dinar nor dirham is accepted; if he has righteous deeds they are taken from him and given to the owner of the wrong, and if he has no righteous deeds the sins of its owner are taken and loaded upon him. An elder with Sa'id said: Did you not hear Abu Hurayra add something in this hadith? He said: No. The elder said: I heard Abu Hurayra add in this hadith that it is said to him: This is the bankrupt."
"2452","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will surely abandon their boasting of the pre-Islamic age, or they will be more contemptible to Allah, mighty and majestic, than beetles."
"2453","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my community, I would command them to perform ablution at every prayer, and siwak with every ablution, and I would delay Isha to midnight."
"2454","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Umari narrated to us, saying: Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, who said: A Bedouin came until he reached the mosque, tied his mount at the mosque door, then entered the mosque and said: Which of you - or: Is among you - the son of Abd al-Muttalib? meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: He is this fair-skinned one reclining. He said: O Muhammad, I will ask you and press my question: I ask you by the Lord of those before you and the Lord of those to come after you - did Allah, mighty and majestic, send you? He said: Yes. He said: I ask you by that - did He command you to pray five prayers in the day and night? He said: Yes. He said: I ask you by that - did He command you to fast a month of twelve months? He said: Yes. He said: I ask you by that - did He command you to perform pilgrimage to the House? He said: Yes. He said: I ask you by that - did He command you to take from the wealth of our rich and return it to our poor? He said: Yes. He said: I have believed in you and affirmed you, and I am the messenger of those behind me of my people; I am Dimam ibn Tha'laba. As for these trivial matters and trifles, we used to leave them out of nobility in the pre-Islamic age. He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to say: I never saw a man more concise than Dimam ibn Tha'laba."
"2455","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The supplication of the wronged is answered, even if he is wicked, for his wickedness is upon himself."
"2456","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the east rose is Friday; Allah, mighty and majestic, guided us to it and led people astray from it: ours is Friday, the Jews' is Saturday, the Christians' is Sunday. In it is an hour - meaning on Friday, which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicated as brief with his hand - in which no servant praying asks for good but is given it."
"2457","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Yaman Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, from Talha ibn Abi Uthman, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, who said: Whoever enters upon food to which he was not invited enters wickedly and eats unlawfully; the worst food is the food of the wedding feast, to which the rich are invited and the poor left out; whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah, mighty and majestic, and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2458","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exchange gifts, for gifts remove the rancor of the chest; let no neighbor belittle her neighbor even with half a sheep's trotter."
"2459","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Umari narrated to us: Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, that a man embraced Islam and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to bathe."
"2460","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant frequents the mosque for prayer and remembrance but Allah, mighty and majestic, rejoices at him when he leaves his family, as the family of an absent one rejoice at their absent one."
"2461","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Fulayh narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, says on the Day of Resurrection: Where are those who loved one another for My majesty? Today I shade them in My shade, a day when there is no shade but My shade."
"2462","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Abu Hurayra, who said: Abu Hurayra bequeathed: When I die, do not pitch a tent over me, do not follow me with fire, and hasten with me; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the believer is placed upon his bier he says: Take me forward, take me forward; when the disbeliever is placed upon his bier he says: Woe to him, where are you taking him."
"2463","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns a fourth time, kill him."
"2464","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: When a believer died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he asked: Is there a debt upon him? If they said: Yes. He said: Did he leave enough to cover his debt? If they said: Yes, he prayed over him; if they said: No, he said: Pray over your companion. When Allah, mighty and majestic, granted us conquests, he said: I am nearer to the believers than themselves; whoever leaves a debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for the heir."
"2465","With the same chain, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, walk with tranquillity upon you; pray what you catch and make up what you miss."
"2466","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah prostrating at (When the heaven splits asunder). I said: Did I not see you prostrate at it, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: If I had not seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate at it, I would not have prostrated."
"2467","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wishes, let him consider what he wishes for, for he does not know what will be decreed for him of his wish."
"2468","And with its chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things, all of them a duty upon the Muslim: visiting the sick, saying Yarhamuk Allah to the one who sneezes when he praises Allah, and following the funeral."
"2469","And with its chain from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave steals, sell him even for a nash."
"2470","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulation, or tribulations; the one sleeping in it will be better than the one awake, the one walking in it will be better than the one hastening, the one sitting in it will be better than the one standing, and the one standing in it will be better than the one walking. So whoever finds in it a refuge or shelter, let him seek refuge in it."
"2471","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is made, Satan turns away passing wind so that he does not hear the call. When the call is finished he comes back, and when the iqamah is pronounced he turns away, and when it is finished he comes back until he whispers between a man and himself, saying: Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such, things he had not remembered, until a person does not know how much he prayed, three or four; so let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting."
"2472","Abu Dawud said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that two women of Hudhayl, one of them threw a stone at the other and killed her and what was in her womb. They disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he assigned for her fetus a ghurrah, a male or female slave, and ruled that the blood money of the woman was upon her Aqilah, and he gave her inheritance and his inheritance to her child and those with them. Then Ibn al-Nabighah al-Hudhali came and said: O Messenger of Allah, must one pay for one who neither ate nor drank, nor spoke nor cried? The like of that is void! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is one of the brothers of the soothsayers, because of the rhymed speech he uttered."
"2473","Abu Dawud said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest."
"2474","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There were among the nations before you men who were spoken to, and if there is any among my Ummah, it is Umar."
"2475","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the punishment of the grave, the punishment of the Fire, the trial of life and death, and the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"2476","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come with calmness upon you; whatever you catch, pray it, and whatever you miss, complete it."
"2477","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah or Aishah, Abu Dawud said: and the doubt is not from me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"2478","Abu Dawud said: Zamah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intense heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so cool the prayer."
"2479","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs of Zuhr then gave the salam. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened? He was told what he had done, so he prayed two rakahs then prostrated two prostrations."
"2480","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad, who said: I heard Abu Salamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was riding a cow, it said: I was not created for this; I was created only for plowing. So I believed in that, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Salamah said: And they were not among the people that day. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was pasturing his sheep, a wolf came and took a sheep from them, and he snatched it from him. It said: How will you deal with her on the day of al-Sabu, the day when there is no shepherd for her but me? So I believed in that, I and Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Salamah said: And they were not among the people that day."
"2481","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw myself in a dream, with people being presented to me wearing shirts; some shirts reaching to such-and-such, and some reaching to such-and-such; and Umar passed by me dragging his shirt. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you interpret that? He said: Religion."
"2482","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf at Mina narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that a Bedouin demanded from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a debt owed to him, and he was harsh to him. The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were about to attack him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for the one who has a right has a say. Then he said: Repay him. They said: We find nothing but a camel better in age than his. He said: Buy it and give it to him, for the best of you are those best in repayment."
"2483","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the frequent female visitors of graves."
"2484","Abu Dawud said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah the Mighty and Majestic has protective jealousy, and the believer has protective jealousy; and the jealousy of Allah the Mighty and Majestic is that the believer commits what He has forbidden him."
"2485","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian or a Magian. Have you not seen the animal giving birth to an animal; do you see in it any mutilated one?"
"2486","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward will be forgiven his past sins, and whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr with faith and seeking reward will be forgiven his past sins."
"2487","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two days, unless it is a man who was fasting a day, then let him fast it."
"2488","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; in it Adam was created, in it the Hour will come, and in it there is an hour in which no servant praying asks Allah the Mighty and Majestic for good but Allah gives it to him. And he made it seem small, and said with his hand like this, that it is brief."
"2489","Abu Dawud said: Hammad narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I came to Sham and met Kab. I would narrate to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would narrate to me from the Torah, until we mentioned Friday. I narrated to him that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim meets asking Allah for good in it but He gives it to him or grants it to him. Kab said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; once in every year? I said: No. He said: Once in every month? I said: No. He said: Once in every Friday? I said: Yes. Abu Hurayrah said: Then I came to Madinah and met Abdullah ibn Salam, and I told him that I had met Kab, and I would narrate to him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would narrate to me from the Torah, until we mentioned Friday, and I mentioned to him what Kab had said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; once in every year. He said: Kab lied. I said: But he retracted. He said: Do you know which hour it is? I said: No, and I pressed him insistently: Tell me, tell me. He said: It is between Asr and Maghrib. I said: And how, when there is no prayer? He said: Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The servant remains in prayer so long as he waits for the prayer; the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him?"
"2490","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, uses the siwak, wears his best clothes, and perfumes himself from his family's perfume, then comes to the mosque and does not step over people's necks, and prays; then when the Imam comes out he listens attentively, it will be an expiation for what is between it and the next Friday."
"2491","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on Friday, Abu Dharr said to Ubayy ibn Kab: When was this surah revealed? He did not answer him. When he finished his prayer he said to him: You have nothing of your prayer except what you engaged in of idle talk. Then Abu Dharr came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: Ubayy has spoken the truth."
"2492","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prefer some of the prophets of Allah over others, or, among the prophets, peace and blessings of Allah be upon them."
"2493","What Ajlan narrated from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile while you are fasting, and if you are standing then sit down. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah the Mighty and Majestic than the scent of musk."
"2494","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel! He said: Ride it, woe to you!"
"2495","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slave is your brother; when he prepares food for you, seat him with you, and if he refuses then feed him, and do not strike their faces."
"2496","Abu al-Walid from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you lead the people in prayer, lighten it, for among them are the young, the old, and the weak."
"2497","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abu al-Walid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor one is not the one whom a morsel or two morsels turn away; rather the poor one is the abstinent one who does not ask people importunately."
"2498","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abu al-Walid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It would not please me to have Uhud in gold, dying the day I die with a dinar of it still with me, except something I set aside for a creditor."
"2499","And what Said ibn Saman narrated from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Saman, freed slave of al-Mushmail, informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Abu Qatadah while he was circumambulating the House, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Maqam, and the first to violate the sanctity of this House will be its own people; when they violate it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Ethiopians will come and destroy it with a destruction after which it will never be inhabited, and they are the ones who will extract its treasure."
"2500","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Saman, who said: Abu Hurayrah came upon us in the mosque of al-Zuraqiyyin and said: The people have abandoned three things which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do: when he entered the prayer he would raise his hands extended, then pause a little asking Allah the Mighty and Majestic of His bounty; and he used to say the takbir when he lowered and raised and when he bowed."
"2501","Nafi ibn Abi Nafi from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Abi Nafi informed us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no wager except in a camel hoof, a horse hoof, or an arrowhead."
"2502","Umar ibn Khaldah from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mutamir narrated to me from Umar ibn Khaldah, who said: We came to Abu Hurayrah concerning a companion of ours who was afflicted, meaning he became bankrupt, and a man found his own goods with him. Abu Hurayrah said: This is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning, that whoever becomes bankrupt or dies, and a man finds his own goods with him, he has more right to them, unless the man leaves enough to pay."
"2503","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah performing ablution on a roof of ours, and I said: O Abu Hurayrah, from what are you performing ablution? He said: From pieces of cheese I ate; indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ablution is due from what fire has touched."
"2504","Abd al-Rahman al-Araj. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl al-Hashimi, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Among the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk, God of truth."
"2505","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, Shubah said: and I know it only from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar and Quraysh, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Ghifar, Aslam, and Ashja are allies of one another; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."
"2506","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come."
"2507","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, Yunus said: I think it is from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The people follow Quraysh in this matter; their Muslims follow their Muslims, and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers."
"2508","Abu Dawud said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from al-Araj, Busr ibn Said, and Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches two rakahs or a rakah of Asr before the sun sets has not missed it, and whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has not missed it."
"2509","And Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"2510","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The people said: O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the sun with no clouds in it? Do you suffer harm in seeing the moon on the night of full moon? They said: No. He said: Likewise you will see Him."
"2511","And al-Agharr Abu Muslim. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels on Friday stand at the door of the mosque writing the first then the first; the one who comes early is like one offering a camel, the one next to him like one offering a cow, the one next to him like one offering a ram, the one next to him like one offering a chicken, and the one next to him like one offering an egg. When the Imam sits on the pulpit, the scrolls are folded, and they sit and listen to the remembrance."
"2512","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard al-Agharr saying: I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic grants respite until a third of the night has passed, then descends and says: Is there any asker? Is there any repentant? Is there any seeker of forgiveness for a sin? A man said to him: Until dawn breaks? He said: Yes."
"2513","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, who said: I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah the Mighty and Majestic but the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic mentions them among those with Him."
"2514","Abu Dawud said: Hammad and Sallam narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted says: Grandeur is My garment, and pride is My cloak; whoever contends with Me for one of them, I shall cast him into Hell."
"2515","And Amir. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Amir narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: They passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a funeral and praised it well, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then they passed with another funeral and praised it evilly, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. And he said: Some of you are witnesses over others."
"2516","Abu al-Jawza. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Jawza, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believing servant is taken, angels of mercy come to him and draw out his soul in white silk, saying: We have not found a scent sweeter than this. They draw him out, saying: Be gentle, for he has come out of the distress of the world. They say: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? He said: As for the disbeliever, his soul comes out, and the keepers of the earth say: We have not found a scent fouler than this, and he is brought down to the lowest earth."
"2517","And Umar ibn Abi Salamah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer is held by his debt until it is paid on his behalf."
"2518","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, or Abu Salamah, Abu Dawud doubted, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will enter Paradise peoples whose hearts are like the hearts of birds."
"2519","And Abu Uthman al-Nahdi. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abbas al-Jurayri, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of the month, Witr before sleep, and the Duha prayer."
"2520","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Uthman, who said: We were with Abu Hurayrah on a journey, and food was brought. We sent for Abu Hurayrah while he was praying, and the messenger came and mentioned that he was fasting. The food was laid out to be eaten, and Abu Hurayrah came when they had almost finished it, and he took from it and began eating. They looked at the man they had sent to Abu Hurayrah, and he said: Why are you looking at me? By Allah, he informed me that he was fasting. He said: He spoke the truth. Then Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month is the fast of a lifetime; so I fast in Allah's multiplication and break fast in His lightening."
"2521","And Abu al-Rabi from Abu Hurayrah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abu al-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, forgive me what I have done before and what I have done after, what I have concealed and what I have declared, and my extravagance, and what You know better than me; You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You."
"2522","Abu Dawud said: Shubah and al-Masudi narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad al-Hadrami, from Abu al-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Four things of the pre-Islamic age the people will never abandon: boasting about lineages, wailing over the dead, seeking rain by stars, and contagion; a camel got mangy and made a hundred mangy; so who made the first camel mangy?"
"2523","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Abu al-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: not to sleep except upon Witr, the Duha prayer, and fasting three days of the month."
"2524","And Shahr ibn Hawshab. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Some Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and mentioned this verse: Uprooted from the surface of the earth, having no stability. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we think it is the truffle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye; and the Ajwah is of Paradise, and it is a cure from poison."
"2525","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Hakam ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Among the worst of people in station is one who destroys his Hereafter for another's world."
"2526","And Abu Salih. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Dhakwan Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women, in prayer."
"2527","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is in prayer so long as the prayer detains him."
"2528","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about what a man speaks to himself of, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is pure faith."
"2529","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith has seventy-odd branches, the best of them the saying there is no god but Allah."
"2530","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday, and forgiveness is granted to whoever does not associate anything with Allah, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity; it is said: Leave these two until they reconcile."
"2531","Abu Dawud said: Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the muezzin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins."
"2532","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child recompenses his father except that he finds him a slave and frees him."
"2533","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you prays after Friday, let him pray four."
"2534","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you consider the martyr among you? They said: The one killed in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my Ummah would be few; whoever is killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, whoever dies in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one who dies of plague is a martyr, and the one who dies of stomach disease is a martyr. Suhayl said: And Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam narrated to me from my father, and I did not hear it from him, that he added in this hadith: And the drowned."
"2535","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst are the last of them; and the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst are the first of them."
"2536","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam and muzaffat. It was said to Abu Hurayrah: What is hantam? He said: Green jars."
"2537","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be encircled with it from seven earths."
"2538","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate a sheep's shoulder, then rinsed his mouth, washed his hand, and prayed."
"2539","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer in his market and in his house by twenty-odd degrees."
"2540","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salih narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"2541","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: I heard Dhakwan narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man performs ablution well, then goes out to prayer, nothing bringing him out or urging him except it, he does not take a step but Allah the Mighty and Majestic raises him a degree by it, or removes a sin from him by it."
"2542","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels invoke blessings upon one of you so long as he remains in his place of prayer, so long as he does not break his ablution, saying: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"2543","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with an iron, his iron will be in his hand stabbing his belly with it on the Day of Resurrection in the Fire of Hell, abiding eternally in it forever; whoever kills himself with poison, his poison will be in his hand sipping it in the Fire of Hell, abiding eternally in it forever; and whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself will be throwing himself down in the Fire of Hell, abiding eternally in it forever."
"2544","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a dog licks the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."
"2545","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash informed me, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he has poured over it once or twice, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"2546","Abu Dawud said: Shubah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves by my name, but do not take my kunyah."
"2547","Abu Dawud said: Shubah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me in wakefulness, for Satan does not take my form. Shubah said: Does not imagine himself in my form."
"2548","Abu Dawud said: Shubah and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, Shubah said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever deliberately lies upon me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2549","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no ablution except from sound or wind."
"2550","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah to Umrah expiates what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"2551","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said concerning the People of the Book: Do not initiate them with the salam, and when you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest part."
"2552","Abu Dawud said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Sumayy the freed slave of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah expiates what is between it and the next Umrah, and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"2553","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb or Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever looks into a people without their permission, they may put out his eye."
"2554","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb or Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not conceal a servant but Allah the Mighty and Majestic will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection."
"2555","Abu Dawud said: Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drought is not that it does not rain for a year; rather drought is that the sky rains but the earth does not produce."
"2556","Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: On the day of Badr the people hastened to the spoils and took them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spoils were not lawful for any dark-headed ones besides you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions, when they gained spoils, would gather them, and fire would descend from heaven and consume them. Then Allah sent down this verse: Were it not for a decree from Allah that preceded, to the end of the two verses."
"2557","Abu Dawud said: Said ibn Sinan Abu Sinan narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed concealing it, then when it is discovered he is pleased by that and admires it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has two rewards: the reward of openness and the reward of secrecy. Abu Bishr said: It was mentioned from Abu Ubayd that it pleased him that no evil deed of his be discovered."
"2558","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays two rakahs, or a rakah, Abu Bishr doubted, of Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."
"2559","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"2560","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; then his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, and a polytheist."
"2561","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has roaming angels of merit who seek gatherings of remembrance. When they come upon people remembering Allah the Mighty and Majestic, they sit and shade them with their wings between them and the lowest heaven. When they rise, they ascend to their Lord, and He, Blessed and Exalted, though knowing best, says: From where have you come? They say: We came from servants of Yours who glorify You, praise You, declare Your oneness, magnify You, seek refuge with You from Your punishment, and ask You for Your Paradise. He, Blessed and Exalted, says: And have they seen My Paradise and My Fire? They say: No. He says: Then how if they had seen them? I have granted them refuge from what they sought refuge from, and given them what they asked for. It is said: Among them is a man who passed by them and sat with them. He says: And to him I have forgiven; they are the people whose companion does not suffer misery."
"2562","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons three consecutive Fridays without excuse, Allah seals his heart."
"2563","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah the Mighty and Majestic loves a servant, He calls Jibril and says: O Jibril, I love so-and-so, so love him. Jibril loves him and calls out in heaven: Allah loves so-and-so, so love him. He said: The people of heaven love him, and acceptance is placed for him on earth. And when He hates a servant, it is likewise."
"2564","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"2565","Abu Dawud said: Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says: The people are ruined, he is the most ruined of them."
"2566","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the Day of Resurrection from the distresses of the Hereafter; whoever eases for a Muslim, Allah will ease for him in this world and the Hereafter; whoever conceals for a Muslim in this world, Allah will conceal for him in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah the Mighty and Majestic is in the aid of the servant so long as he is in the aid of his brother."
"2567","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid, and he was trustworthy, narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih al-Madani narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no owner of treasure who does not pay its zakat but he and his treasure will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and plates of the Fire of Hell will be heated, and his forehead, brow, and back will be branded with them, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count; then he will see his path either to Paradise or to the Fire. There is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakat but he and his camels will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest state, and a flat plain will be spread for them, and they will trample him with their hooves; whenever the last of them passes, the first will be returned upon him, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, and he will see his path either to Paradise or to the Fire. There is no owner of sheep who does not pay their zakat but he and his sheep will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest state, and a flat plain will be spread for them, and they will butt him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; whenever the last of them passes, the first will be returned upon him, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, and he will see his path either to Paradise or to the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about horses? He said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection; horses are of three kinds: for one man a reward, for one man a covering, and upon another a burden. As for the one for whom it is a reward, a man keeps them tied in the path of Allah the Mighty and Majestic, so whatever is hidden in their bellies is a reward for him; if he pastures them in a meadow and lengthens their rope, he has a reward for all they hide in their bellies; if they run a hill or two, he has a reward for every step they take or are made to take; if he passes with them by a river and waters them from it, he has a reward for every drop they hide in their bellies, until he mentioned the reward in their dung and urine. As for the one for whom it is a covering, a man takes them for abstinence, dignity, and adornment, and does not forget their right in their backs and bellies, in hardship and ease. As for the one upon whom it is a burden, a man takes them for pride, arrogance, and showing off to people. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about donkeys? He said: Nothing was sent down to me concerning them except this comprehensive verse: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it."
"2568","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Khaybar: I shall surely give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, through whom victory will come. Umar said: I never loved leadership before that day, so I stretched toward it and looked expectantly, hoping it would be given to me. When the next day came, he called Ali and gave it to him, saying: Fight, and do not turn until Allah the Mighty and Majestic grants you victory. He went a little then said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall I fight? He said: Until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His Messenger; when they do that, they have protected their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"2569","And Abdullah ibn Rabah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rabah, who said: We came as a delegation to Muawiyah, and with us was Abu Hurayrah. Some of us would prepare food for others, and Abu Hurayrah was among those who prepared for us abundantly, inviting us to his lodging. I said: If I ordered food to be prepared and invited them to my lodging. So I did, and I met Abu Hurayrah in the evening and said: O Abu Hurayrah, the invitation is at my place tonight. He said: You beat me to it, O brother of the Ansar. I invited them; while they were with me, Abu Hurayrah said: Shall I not inform you of a hadith of your hadith, O company of Ansar? Abdullah ibn Rabah was an Ansari. He said: He mentioned the conquest of Makkah, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid over one flank, Zubayr over the other flank, and Abu Ubaydah over the unarmored foot soldiers. Then he saw me and said: O Abu Hurayrah. I said: At your service and happiness, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Call out the Ansar, and bring me none but an Ansari. He said: I did. Then he said: Look to Quraysh and their rabble; mow them down mowing. He said: We set out; none of them directed anything at us, and none of us wanted any of them but took him. Abu Sufyan came and said: O Messenger of Allah, the green multitude of Quraysh has perished; there is no Quraysh after today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe, and whoever lays down arms is safe. The people laid down their arms, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, beginning with the Stone, touching it, then circumambulating seven times, and praying two rakahs behind the Maqam. Then he came, with a bow in his hand holding its grip, and began striking with it the eye of one of their idols, saying: Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing. Then he went until he came to al-Safa, ascending it until he could see the House, glorifying Allah and supplicating Him. The Ansar were with him, saying: As for the man, longing for his town has seized him, and pity for his kin. Revelation came; and when the truth came, it was not hidden from us. When the revelation was lifted, he said: O company of Ansar, you said: As for the man, longing for his town has seized him, and pity for his kin. No; then what would my name be? No; I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; life is your life, and death is your death. They came weeping, saying: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah we said it only out of possessiveness for Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His Messenger believe you and excuse you."
"2570","Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freed slave of the family of Talhah, from Isa ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu form, who said: No eye that wept from fear of Allah the Mighty and Majestic will enter the Fire until milk returns to the udder, and the smoke of Hell and dust in the path of Allah do not gather in the nostrils of a servant, or the foot of a Muslim."
"2571","And Abu Rafi. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, who said: I heard Abu Rafi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that he prostrated at When the heaven splits asunder, saying: I saw my close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating at it, and I shall keep prostrating until I meet him."
"2572","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, who said: I heard Abu Rafi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The name of Maymunah or Zaynab was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named her Maymunah or Zaynab."
"2573","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Abu Amir al-Khazzaz Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that a black man or black woman used to remove filth from the mosque and was buried, and they did not inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of that and said: Show me her grave. He went to the grave, came to the graves and said: These graves are filled with darkness upon their people, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic illuminates them for them by my prayer. Then he came to the grave and prayed over it. A man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, my father, or my brother, has died and been buried, so pray over him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with the Ansari."
"2574","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Fayruz narrated to us, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of the month, Witr before sleep, and the two rakahs of Duha."
"2575","Abu Dawud said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is in prayer so long as he remains in the place where he prayed, waiting for the prayer; the angels say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him, so long as he does not break his ablution."
"2576","Abu Dawud said: Shubah and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When he sits between her four parts, then exerts himself, ghusl has become obligatory. He said: And Hammad ibn Salamah added in this hadith: Whether he emits or does not emit."
"2577","And Bashir ibn Nahik. Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas narrating from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man becomes bankrupt and a man finds his own goods with him, he has more right to them."
"2578","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man frees a share of his belonging from a slave, he is free."
"2579","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who heard al-Nadr, who heard Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the gold ring."
"2580","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Umra is permissible."
"2581","Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two wives and inclines to one of them will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen."
"2582","Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Golden locusts rained upon Ayyub, peace be upon him, and he began taking from them. It was revealed to him: O Ayyub, did I not enrich you? He said: O Lord, who can ever be satiated of Your mercy or Your bounty?"
"2583","Kumayl ibn Ziyad. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Kumayl ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except by Allah, and there is no refuge nor escape from Him except to Him."
"2584","And Abu Murayah. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Murayah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angels do not invoke blessings upon a wailing woman nor a singing woman."
"2585","And Zurarah ibn Awfa. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her until morning, or until she returns, Abu Dawud doubted."
"2586","Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Zurarah ibn Awfa narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic has pardoned for my Ummah what their souls speak of, so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it."
"2587","And Hilal ibn Yazid. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed me, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Yazid narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the black seed: In it is a cure for every disease except death. He said: Meaning shuniz. Qatadah says it."
"2588","And al-Qaqa. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Safwan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Miserliness and faith do not gather in the heart of a servant."
"2589","And Hafs ibn Asim. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven are in the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade but His shade: a just ruler, a just imam, a youth raised in the worship of Allah, a man whose heart is attached to the mosque until he returns to it, two men who meet upon the love of Allah and part upon His love, a man who gives charity concealing it until his left hand does not know what his right hand conceals, a man whom a woman of rank and beauty calls and he says: I fear Allah, and a man who remembers Allah alone and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"2590","Abu Dawud said: al-Umari narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and no prayer after Fajr until the sun rises."
"2591","And al-Hasan al-Basri from Abu Hurayrah. Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only one who hopes not to wear it in the Hereafter wears silk in this world; only one with no share wears silk."
"2592","Abu Dawud said: Abu Hilal Muhammad ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Musa, peace be upon him, saying: Out of his modesty he would not bathe except covered."
"2593","Abu Dawud said: Jasr Abu Jafar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who wakes at night, or upon his bed, and says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, O Allah forgive me, but he is forgiven. If he resolves, rises, performs ablution, prays, and supplicates Allah, He answers him."
"2594","Abu Dawud said: Jasr narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Ya Sin in a night seeking the Face of Allah is forgiven."
"2595","Abu Dawud said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, who said: A man came to Madinah and met Abu Hurayrah. Abu Hurayrah said to him: As if you are not of the people of the town. He said: Yes. He said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Allah may benefit you by it? He said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing a servant will be reckoned for on the Day of Resurrection is prayer. Allah the Mighty and Majestic says to His angels: Look into his prayer; did he complete it or diminish it? They look; if it is complete it is written complete, and if something was diminished from it, He says: Complete for My servant his obligation from his voluntary deeds. Then deeds are taken accordingly. Abu Dawud said: And I heard an elder in the Sacred Mosque narrating this hadith. He said: Al-Hasan said, while in the gathering of Abu Hurayrah when he narrated this hadith: By Allah, this is better for the son of Adam than the world and what is in it."
"2596","Abu Dawud said: Abbad ibn Maysarah al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, who said: While Abu Hurayrah was narrating to the people, a youth came wearing two garments and stood over him, saying: What do you say about letting my lower garment trail? Or about dragging my lower garment? He said: I heard my close truthful friend, Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: There was among those before you a man strutting in his two cloaks, or between his two garments, when Allah caused the earth to swallow him; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, he sinks in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"2597","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The five prayers and Friday to Friday are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are avoided."
"2598","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things I shall never abandon: bathing on Friday, Witr before sleep, and fasting three days of the month."
"2599","Abu Dawud said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, while we were then in Madinah, who said: Islam will come on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: You are Islam, and I am al-Salam; today by you I give, and by you I take."
"2600","Abd al-Rahman ibn Haddad. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Haddad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Maiz ibn Malik came to Hazzal and said: The other has committed adultery. He said: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him before a Quran comes down concerning you. He said: He went to him and informed him until he testified four times, so he ordered him stoned and he was stoned. Two men passed by him saying: Woe to this one; Allah concealed him, but he did not conceal himself, and was driven like a dog is driven. They came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a carcass; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bite from this carcass. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a carcass and we cannot bear it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What you have taken from your brother is fouler than this; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I have seen him wading in a river of Paradise. And he said: Would that you had shown him mercy, O Hazzal."
"2601","And Abdullah al-Awdi. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abdullah al-Awdi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what most admits people into the Fire? He said: The two hollows: the private part and the mouth. It was said: What most admits people into Paradise? He said: Taqwa of Allah and good character."
"2602","And Ammar ibn Abi Ammar. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I never witnessed spoils with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he apportioned to me from them, except Khaybar, for it was exclusively for the people of Hudaybiyah. Abu Musa and Abu Hurayrah had come between Hunayn and Hudaybiyah."
"2603","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines; the best of them in pre-Islamic times are the best of them in Islam, when they understand."
"2604","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Peoples will leave Madinah, though Madinah is better for them if they knew."
"2605","And Abd al-Malik. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given wealth without asking, let him accept it, for it is provision Allah the Mighty and Majestic has provided him."
"2606","And Umayr, freed slave of Banu Adi. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Umayr, freed slave of Banu Adi, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran before sleeping? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who can bear a third of the Quran before sleeping? He said: He recites: Say, He is Allah, One, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and Say, I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind, and it is as if he recited a third of the Quran."
"2607","And Abu Abdullah al-Qarraaz. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarraaz, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hypocrite does not maintain forty nights upon the last Isha prayer, meaning in congregation."
"2608","And Muhammad ibn Ziyad. Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured to you, count thirty."
"2609","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Qurashi informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: al-Hasan ibn Ali took a date of charity and put it in his mouth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kikh, kakh, throw it away; do you not know that we do not eat charity?"
"2610","Abu Dawud said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abul Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her; and Aslam, may Allah grant her peace."
"2611","2606 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the people took a valley or a mountain pass, and the Ansar took a mountain pass or a valley, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar. Abu Hurayrah said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for him, he did them no wrong; they indeed shared their wealth with him, sheltered him and aided him."
"2612","2607 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, blessed and exalted is He, said: Every deed is an expiation except fasting; it is Mine and I reward for it, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, than the scent of musk."
"2613","2608 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah; and he came upon some people performing ablution from the ablution vessel, and he said: Perform ablution thoroughly, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"2614","2609 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah, who heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, does not look at one who drags his lower garment out of pride."
"2615","2610 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"2616","2611 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, who heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wear both sandals together, or take off both together; when you put on footwear begin with the right, and when you take off begin with the left."
"2617","2612 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah, who heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Does not the one who raises his head before the imam fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey."
"2618","2613 - Abu Dawud said: al-Rabi' ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who does not thank people does not thank Allah."
"2619","2614 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who heard Abu Hurayrah, who heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever buys a sheep whose milk has been withheld in its udder has the choice; if he returns it, he returns along with it a sa' of dates."
"2620","2615 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The freed slaves were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I trust them more than I trust you, or than some of you."
"2621","2616 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sulaym Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise beneath the Throne? There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"2622","2617 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wishes to find the taste of faith, let him love a servant only for the sake of Allah."
"2623","2618 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman, the brother of Abu Hurrah, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: A man called out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"2624","2619 - Abu Dawud said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is an hour on Friday that no Muslim man coincides with while in prayer - or he said: praying - asking Allah, mighty and majestic is He, for something therein - or he said: for good - except that He grants it to him. And he gestured with his hand like this; Abu Dawud turned his hand over and back. We said: He is making it seem brief. We said: He is deeming it short."
"2625","2620 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is an hour on Friday that no servant coincides with while standing in prayer, asking Allah therein for good, except that He grants it to him."
"2626","2621 - Abu Dawud said: Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, prostrated at: {When the sky splits apart} and {Read in the name of your Lord who created}, and one who is better than them both."
"2627","2622 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Placing the hands on the waist during prayer was forbidden."
"2628","2623 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until some people of my nation return to idols worshipping them besides Allah."
"2629","2624 - Abu Dawud said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: Whoever loves me, let him love these two."
"2630","2625 - Abu Dawud said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is from the direction of the East."
"2631","2626 - Abu Dawud said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None has been given power over killing the Dajjal except Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him."
"2632","2627 - Abu Dawud said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man had Uhud in gold and spent it in the path of Allah, and on widows, the needy and orphans, to attain the merit of one of my Companions for an hour of the day, he would never attain it."
"2633","2628 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr - or Umar - ibn Abd al-Rahman - Abu Dawud said: one of the two - that Abu Basrah al-Ghifari met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming, and said: From where have you come? He said: I have come from al-Tur, where I prayed. He said: Indeed, had I met you I would not have let you go, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Journeys are undertaken only to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"2634","2629 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrating from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a man becomes bankrupt, and a man finds his goods intact with him, he has more right to them than the other creditors."
"2635","2630 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Malik ibn Zalim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The destruction of my nation will be at the hands of foolish young boys of Quraysh."
"2636","2631 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mahri, that Abu Hurayrah said to him: O Mahri, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper, the earnings of the prostitute, the price of the dog, and the stud fee of the stallion."
"2637","2632 - Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id al-Mahri narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best ribat is waiting for prayer and adhering to gatherings of remembrance; and there is no servant who prays then sits in his place except that the angels continue to invoke blessings upon him until he breaks his ablution or stands up."
"2638","2633 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Mas'ud, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There was a man who lent to people, and he used to say to his servant: When the insolvent one is unable to pay, overlook him; perhaps Allah will overlook us. So when he met Allah, mighty and majestic is He, He overlooked him."
"2639","2634 - Abu Dawud said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen, and the best of omens is the good omen. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the good omen? He said: The good word that one of you hears."
"2640","2635 - Abu Dawud said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani and from Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she repeats, let him flog her; if she repeats, let him flog her; if she repeats a fourth time, let him sell her even for a braid of hair."
"2641","2636 - Abu Dawud said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Khalid and from Abu Hurayrah, they said: Two litigants came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you to judge between us by the Book of Allah. Then his opponent, who was more understanding than him, stood and said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me to speak. He permitted him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, my son was a hired laborer for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son deserved stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then when I asked the people of knowledge, they informed me that upon my son is a hundred lashes and banishment for a year, and that upon this man's wife is stoning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose Hand is my soul, I shall surely judge between you by the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic is He. As for the hundred sheep and the servant, they are returned to you; upon your son is a hundred lashes and banishment for a year. Go, O Unays, to this man's wife; if she confesses, stone her. So he went to her in the morning and asked her, and she confessed, and he stoned her."
"2642","2637 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Abu Zur'ah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike shikal in horses."
"2643","2638 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ja'far, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a third of the night remains, He, blessed and exalted is He, says: Who is it that seeks the removal of harm so I may remove it from him? Who is it that seeks provision from Me so I may provide for him? Who is it that asks Me so I may give him?"
"2644","2639 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Ja'far, who heard Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three supplications are answered: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a father for his child."
"2645","2640 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Ja'far, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best deeds on the Day of Resurrection are faith in which there is no doubt, striving in which there is no misappropriation of spoils, and an accepted Hajj. Abu Hurayrah said: An accepted Hajj expiates the sins of that year."
"2646","2641 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sayyar and Mansur, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever performs Hajj and does not engage in obscenity nor commit sin, returns as on the day his mother gave birth to him."
"2647","2642 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah informed me, he said: I heard Abu Hazim narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slave girls."
"2648","2643 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, he said: I heard Abu Hazim narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"2649","2644 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi, who heard Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Going out to meet traders was forbidden - or he forbade going out to meet them - and that a townsman sell for a bedouin."
"2650","2645 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi, who heard Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Tasriyah, najsh, a woman asking for the divorce of her sister so she may take what is in her bowl, and a man proposing over the proposal of his brother were forbidden. Abu Dawud said: As though by his saying 'he forbade' he means the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2651","2646 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the rulers, woe to the trustees, woe to the headmen; on the Day of Resurrection some people will wish that their forelocks had been suspended from the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had never undertaken any office."
"2652","2647 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a burden of dependents, it is upon me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for the heirs. Abu Bishr said: I heard Abu al-Walid saying: This abrogated those hadiths that came concerning abandoning prayer over one who owed a debt."
"2653","2648 - Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong is not one who throws people down or overcomes people; rather the strong is one who overcomes his own self."
"2654","2649 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Ali, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Soothsaying, its beginning is blame and its end is regret, and the punishment on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I said: O Abu Hurayrah, except one among them who fears Allah? He said: I only narrate to you as I heard."
"2655","2650 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dinar, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak ibn Malik al-Ghifari, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity due on the horse of a Muslim nor on his slave boy."
"2656","2651 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik al-Ghifari, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity due on the horse of a Muslim nor on his slave boy."
"2657","2652 - Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: He wrote it to me and I read it to him; he heard Abu Uthman from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the occupant of this chamber, the truthful one believed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Mercy is not removed except from a wretched one."
"2658","2653 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, who heard Abu Uthman from Abu Hurayrah; Shu'bah said: I do not know whether he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or said: from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night voluntarily, other than the obligatory, a house is built for him in Paradise. Abu Dawud said: And this too is among what Mansur wrote to him."
"2659","2654 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus son of Matta."
"2660","2655 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I came out to you while the Night of Decree and the false messiah had been made clear to me; then there was a quarrel between two men in the mosque, so I went to separate them, and it was made forgotten to me. I shall give you a hint of them: as for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten nights in the odd ones; as for the false messiah, he is blind in one eye, with a clear forehead, broad chest, in him is a stoop, like Qatan ibn Abd al-Uzza. A man said: Will his resemblance harm me, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, you are a Muslim and he is a disbeliever."
"2661","2656 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy, do not pry, do not sever ties, do not turn away from one another, do not hate one another; and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"2662","2657 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Zadham narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever memorizes knowledge then is asked about it and conceals it, will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"2663","2658 - Abu Dawud said: Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, visit occasionally and love will increase."
"2664","2659 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abi Suwayd, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teach and do not be harsh, for the teacher is better than the harsh one."
"2665","2660 - Abu Dawud said: A shaykh of the people of Makkah narrated to me, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep fasting chaste, for fasting is not merely from food nor from drink; rather fasting is from sins. So when one of you fasts and a man behaves ignorantly toward him or insults him, let him say: I am fasting."
"2666","2661 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the two black ones in prayer, meaning the snake and the scorpion."
"2667","2662 - Abu Dawud said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Damdam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the two black ones in prayer: the snake and the scorpion."
"2668","2663 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrating from Abu al-Mutawwis - Habib said: I had seen Abu al-Mutawwis - from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever breaks fast on a day of Ramadan without a concession that Allah granted him, fasting the entire year will never make up for it."
"2669","2664 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Isa, peace be upon him, will remain on earth after he descends for forty years, then he will die, and the Muslims will pray over him and bury him."
"2670","2665 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Uthman - Shu'bah said: he used to call the adhan on the tallest minaret in Kufah - he said: Abu Yahya narrated to me while I was circumambulating with him - meaning around the House - he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying - I heard it from his mouth: The mu'adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry bears witness for him; the one who witnesses the prayer has twenty-five good deeds recorded for him, and what is between them is expiated."
"2671","2666 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The womb has a tongue on the Day of Resurrection beneath the Throne saying: O Lord, I have been severed; O Lord, I have been wronged; O Lord, I have been treated badly. So its Lord answers it: Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you, and sever whoever severs you?"
"2672","2667 - Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to sit upon a live coal is better for him than to sit upon a grave. Abu Hurayrah said: Meaning: to sit to relieve himself of stool or urine."
"2673","2668 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Night of Decree: It is the night of the twenty-seventh - or twenty-ninth - and the angels on that night on earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles."
"2674","2669 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: O Allah, love them and love whoever loves them."
"2675","2670 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahhak, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it, and it is the tree of eternity."
"2676","2671 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was named al-Khadir only because he sat in a place and it shook with greenery."
"2677","2672 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Allah ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hasten to do deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its west, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast of the earth, the private affair of one of you, and the general affair."
"2678","2673 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them - and Allah knows whether he mentioned the third or not - then there will come people who love corpulence and bear witness before they are asked to bear witness."
"2679","2674 - Abu Dawud said: al-Bara' ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are the weak, the oppressed. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every harsh, arrogant one; they are those who do not feel pain in their heads."
"2680","2675 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, he said: Ibn Abbas addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined two prayers, meaning Maghrib and Isha. Something of it remained in my mind until I met Abu Hurayrah and asked him, and he confirmed him."
"2681","2676 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'd al-Shami, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Words I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I shall not abandon: O Allah, make me increase in Your remembrance, magnify gratitude to You, follow Your counsel, and preserve Your command."
"2682","2677 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sufyan al-Tamimi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I suffered severe hunger, so I prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I intercepted Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, so he took my hand; I asked him about a verse of the Qur'an which I knew better than him. I walked with him until he reached his house, hoping he would admit me and give me supper. When he reached the house he released his hand from mine and entered. Then I intercepted Umar and he did the same to me. Then I intercepted Ali ibn Abi Talib and asked him about what I had asked them about, concerning a verse of the Qur'an. When we reached the house he said: Enter, O Abu Hurayrah, and have supper. So I entered, and he said: O Fatimah, give Abu Hurayrah supper. He entered the privy and stayed long therein, as he used to do. She called me for a round loaf, so I ate; then she called me for sawiq, so I drank. Ali came out and said: O Fatimah, did you give Abu Hurayrah supper? She said: Yes. That reached Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, and he said: By Allah, for me to have undertaken of that what he undertook is dearer to me than red camels - or he said: dearer to me than what the sun rises upon."
"2683","2678 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id al-Duba'i narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bushayr ibn Ka'b al-Adawi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you differ concerning the road, make it seven cubits."
"2684","2679 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"2685","2680 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Ubayd, the freedman of Abu Ruhm, narrating that Abu Hurayrah saw a woman on one of the roads of Madinah, and the scent of perfume wafted from her. Abu Hurayrah said to her: Do you intend the mosque? She said: Yes. He said: Did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no woman who perfumes herself for the mosque whose prayer Allah, mighty and majestic is He, accepts until she washes from it as she washes from janabah, so go back. He said: Then I saw her turning away."
"2686","2681 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face."
"2687","2682 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa' narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, said: I am the most self-sufficient of partners; whoever associates with Me, his little and his much belong to him."
"2688","2683 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa Abu al-Mughirah of Banu Sulaym narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hospitality is three days; what is beyond that is charity. So let the guest depart, and let him not burden the household."
"2689","2684 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa' narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Sa'ib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is defective, it is defective."
"2690","2685 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands extended, meaning in prayer."
"2691","2686 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who hears wisdom and narrates only the worst of what he heard is like one to whom it is said: Enter the enclosure and take the fattest sheep in it, and he comes out leading a dog."
"2692","2687 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The beast of the earth will emerge with the staff of Musa and the seal of Sulayman; it will brand the nose of the disbeliever with the staff, and brighten the face of the believer with the seal, until people gather at the table, the believer distinguished from the disbeliever."
"2693","2688 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On Friday the angels are at the doors of the mosque writing people according to their stations: So-and-so came at such-and-such hour; so-and-so came while the imam was delivering the sermon; so-and-so came and attained the prayer but did not attain Friday."
"2694","2689 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Aws, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in three categories: riders, walkers, and on their faces. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, will they walk on their faces? He said: The One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces."
"2695","2690 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Amir al-Uqayli, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first three to enter Paradise and the first three to enter the Fire were shown to me. As for the first three to enter Paradise: the martyr, a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and is sincere to his master, and a poor, chaste one with dependents. As for the first three to enter the Fire: an oppressive ruler, a wealthy one who does not give the right of his wealth, and a poor, boastful one."
"2696","2691 - Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Abu Kathir al-Ghubari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted, or their sale is with a choice."
"2697","2692 - Abu Dawud said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, from Abu Kathir al-Suhaymi, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is from these two trees, from the date palm and the grapevine."
"2698","2693 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a duty upon every Muslim to bathe every seven days as he bathes from janabah, washing his body and his head, making that on Friday."
"2699","2694 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Ibn Burthun, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and majestic is He, prescribed Friday upon those before us, but they differed concerning it, so Allah guided us to it; thus Saturday is for the Jews and Sunday is for the Christians."
"2700","2695 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Ali, that a man said to Abu Hurayrah: Ali ibn Abi Talib recited in Friday prayer with al-Jumu'ah and {When the hypocrites come to you}. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"2701","2696 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Wardan informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man follows the religion of his close friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends."
"2702","2697 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Farqad al-Sabakhi, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most lying of people are the dyers and the goldsmiths."
"2703","2698 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their mothers are different but their religion is one. I am the most entitled of people to Isa son of Maryam, for there was no prophet between me and him. When you see him, recognize him: he is a man of medium stature inclining to redness and whiteness, between two garments dyed yellowish, as though his head drips though no wetness touched it. He will break the cross, kill the pig, and wealth will overflow, until Allah destroys in his time all religions except Islam, and until Allah destroys in his time the false messiah, the blind liar. Security will prevail on earth until the lion grazes with camels, the tiger with cattle, wolves with sheep, children play with snakes, and none harms another. Then he will remain on earth for forty years, then die, and the Muslims will pray over him and bury him."
"2704","2699 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Yazid Abu al-Hasan al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Harim narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about prayer and its times, and he said: Abu Hurayrah claimed that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward Makkah, during travel and residence in Makkah until they returned, two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."
"2705","2700 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah; whoever obeys the commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me. If he prays sitting, then pray sitting; when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise; and when he recites: {Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray}, say: Amin, for when the speech of the people of heaven coincides with the speech of the people of earth, the servant is forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"2706","2701 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from five: from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the false messiah."
"2707","2702 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah - Shu'bah said: And Yunus ibn Khabbab narrated to me, having heard Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, though Ya'la did not raise it to Abu Hurayrah - he said: Whoever says: I ask Allah for Paradise seven times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge from the Fire, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire."
"2708","2703 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la, he said: I heard Abu Alqamah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Khosrau perishes there will be no Khosrau after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him."
"2709","2704 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, he said: I heard al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits until it is finished has two qirats. Ibn Umar disapproved of that, so they sent to A'ishah and asked her, and she said: He spoke the truth. That reached Abu Hurayrah, and he said: Neither the transactions of the market nor the planting of palm saplings distracted me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I only kept close to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a word he would teach me, or a morsel he would feed me."
"2710","2705 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, he said: I heard Amr ibn Asim al-Thaqafi saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, command me something to say when I wake in the morning and when I enter the evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and from the evil of Satan and his association. Say it when you wake in the morning, when you enter the evening, and when you take your bed."
"2711","2706 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Ta'i, he said: Abu al-Mudillah, the freedman of the Mother of the Believers, narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you our hearts soften and we are of the people of the Hereafter; but when we leave you and smell women and children, the world pleases us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you remained - or: if you were - when you leave me as you are when with me, the angels would shake hands with you with their palms and visit you in your houses. And if you did not sin, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, would bring a people who sin so they may seek forgiveness and He may forgive them. We said: O Messenger of Allah, inform us of Paradise, what is its construction? He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver, its mortar is pungent musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, its soil is saffron. Whoever enters it enjoys bliss and never suffers, lives forever and never dies; his garments never wear out and his youth never perishes."
"2712","2707 - Abu Dawud said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Ta'i, he said: Abu al-Mudillah narrated to me, who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose supplication is not rejected: the just ruler, the fasting one until he breaks his fast, and the supplication of the oppressed is carried upon the clouds, the doors of heaven are opened for it, and the Lord, mighty and majestic is He, says: By My might, I shall surely aid you even after a while."
"2713","2708 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is more noble to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, than supplication."
"2714","2709 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Wasi' narrated to us, from Sumayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord, mighty and majestic is He, said: If My servants obeyed Me, I would give them rain by night, bring out the sun upon them by day, and not let them hear the sound of thunder."
"2715","2710 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was in a desert, he heard thunder in a cloud, and heard therein speech: Water the garden of So-and-so, by his name. That cloud came to a lava field and emptied therein what water it had. Then it came to the end of a watercourse, ending at a channel, which absorbed the water. The man walked with the cloud until he reached a man standing in his garden watering it. He said: O servant of Allah, what is your name? He said: Why do you ask? He said: I heard in a cloud - this being its water - : Water the garden of So-and-so, by your name. What do you do with it when you harvest it? He said: Since you have said that, I make it into three thirds: I make a third for me and my family, return a third into it, and make a third for the needy, beggars and travelers."
"2716","2711 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he was in the mosque when the mu'adhdhin called the adhan and a man left. Abu Hurayrah said: As for this one, he has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us, when we hear the call, not to leave the mosque until we pray."
"2717","2712 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was large in the palms and large in the feet."
"2718","2713 - Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khuthaym ibn Irak, that Abu Hurayrah and a group of his people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a delegation, and found that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had gone out to Khaybar. He said: So we set out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him having conquered Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to the people, and they included us in their shares."
"2719","2714 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, he said: One who heard Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, narrating to Sa'id ibn al-As that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Aban ibn Sa'id in an expedition toward Najd. They returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Khaybar, having conquered it. Aban said: Allot to us. I said: We shall not allot to them, O Messenger of Allah. Aban said to me: You are here indeed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit, O Aban. And he did not allot to them."
"2720","2715 - Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from a cousin of theirs who used to narrate much to them, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and there is nothing before him to screen him, let him draw a line, and whatever passes before him will not harm him."
"2721","2716 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah saying: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with three and forbade me from three: he commanded me with the two rak'ahs of Duha, fasting three days of the month, and Witr before sleep; and he forbade me from three: turning in prayer like the turning of the fox, squatting like the squatting of the monkey, and pecking like the pecking of the rooster."
"2722","2717 - Abu Dawud said: Jahir ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abbas ibn Hulays, from a man of the people of Kufah, he said: I was in the circle of Abu Hurayrah, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever testifies against a servant with a testimony he does not deserve, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"2723","2718 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard an elder of Balharith narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: It is not I who forbade people from fasting on Friday; rather I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not fast on Friday unless you fast a day before it or a day after it. And it is not I who prayed in sandals; rather I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in sandals."
"2724","2719 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from one who heard Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Woe to you - or: woe unto you - ride it."
"2725","2720 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umayr ibn Asid ibn Jariyah, the ally of Banu Zuhrah, who was among the companions of Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ten men as spies, and appointed over them Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aqlah, the grandfather of Asim ibn Umar. They set out until, when they were at al-Had'ah between Usfan and Makkah, they were reported to a clan of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. They mobilized for them a hundred archers and followed their tracks until they found their meal of dates, and said: These are dates of Yathrib. When Asim and his companions sensed them, they took refuge on a hill. They said: Come down, and you have the covenant and pledge that we shall not kill any of you. Asim said: As for me, I shall not come down under the protection of a disbeliever today. O Allah, convey greetings from us to our Prophet. So they fought them; seven of them were killed, and three came down under the covenant and pledge. When they gained power over them, they untied the strings of their bows and bound them. When one of the three saw that from them, he said: By Allah, this is the first treachery. They struggled with him and killed him. They set out with Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah, taking them to Makkah, and sold them - that being after the battle of Badr. The sons of al-Harith bought Khubayb, who had killed al-Harith on the day of Badr. The daughter of al-Harith said: Khubayb was a captive with us; by Allah, I never saw a captive better than Khubayb. By Allah, I saw him eating a bunch of grapes though there was no fruit in Makkah that day; it was only provision that Allah, mighty and majestic is He, provided to Khubayb. She said: He borrowed from me a razor to shave with for the killing. She said: So I lent it to him, and a son of mine crawled while I was unaware, and I saw him seating him on his chest. She said: I was frightened with a fright that Khubayb perceived. She said: He noticed me and said: Do you think I shall kill him? I would never do it. She said: When they gathered to kill him, he said to them: Let me pray two rak'ahs. She said: So he prayed two rak'ahs, then said: Were it not that you would think I am afraid, I would have added. He said: Khubayb was the first to institute prayer for one killed in captivity. Then he said: O Allah, count them in number, kill them separately, and leave none of them. Then he recited: ""Ubali shilw ..."" [verse truncated in the printed source]. He said: The polytheists sent to Asim ibn Thabit to be brought some of his flesh, for he had killed a man of their notables. Allah, mighty and majestic is He, sent a cloud-like swarm of hornets that protected him from their messengers, so they could not take anything of his flesh."
"2726","2721 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: One of the daughters-in-law of Marwan died, so Marwan and Abu Hurayrah attended the funeral with him. He said: Marwan heard women weeping and berated them, or shouted at them. Abu Hurayrah said to him: O Abu Abd al-Malik, we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, and Umar saw women weeping and seized them, or shouted at them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umar, leave them, for the eye weeps, the soul is afflicted, and the covenant is recent."
"2727","2722 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tamimi narrated to us, from Isa ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, in a raised narration, he said: The good omens of horses are in their chestnut ones."
"2728","2723 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jahdam Musa ibn Salim, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: It was said to him: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) single you out with something he did not generalize to people? He said: No, except three: he commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly, not to eat charity, and not to mate a donkey upon a mare."
"2729","2724 - Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi, from his mother, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not stare at them, meaning the lepers."
"2730","2725 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hisham narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, that a man asked Ibn Abbas about a man who bought goods: may he sell them before taking possession? Ibn Abbas said: As for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, it is food. Ibn Abbas said: And I deem everything like food."
"2731","2726 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded - or: your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has been commanded - to prostrate upon seven bones, and not to tuck up a garment nor hair."
"2732","2727 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, he said: The most knowledgeable of them of that narrated to me - meaning Ibn Abbas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For one of you to grant his brother a loan of land is better."
"2733","2728 - Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who had changed his white hair, and said: This is good. Then he saw a man who had dyed his beard red, and said: This is better than the first. Then he saw a man who had dyed his beard yellow, and said: This is better than all of that."
"2734","2729 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed for the people of Madinah Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd Qarn, and for the people of Yemen Yalamlam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the appointed places for their people, and for everyone who comes upon them from other than their people, for whoever intends Hajj and Umrah. Whoever is nearer than that, then from where he begins; likewise, until the people of Makkah enter ihram from Makkah."
"2735","2730 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make things easy and do not make them hard; and when one of you becomes angry, let him be silent."
"2736","2731 - Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the fixed shares to their rightful owners; what remains is for the nearest male relative."
"2737","2732 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, who heard Jabir ibn Zayd, who heard Ibn Abbas, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon at Arafat, saying: Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a lower garment, let him wear trousers."
"2738","2733 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram. Amr said: Jabir said to me: We deem her to be Maymunah."
"2739","2734 - Abu Dawud said: Habib ibn Yazid al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Harim narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about prayer and its times, and he said: Ibn Abbas used to say: The time of the dawn prayer is from the rising of dawn until the rays of the sun rise. Whoever is heedless of it, let him not pray until it rises and its horns depart. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled by night then halted at the end of the night, and did not wake until the sun rose or part of it; so he did not pray until it had risen high."
"2740","2735 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in Madinah seven together and eight together."
"2741","2736 - Abu Dawud said: Habib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir, that Ibn Abbas combined Zuhr and Asr due to preoccupation, and Ibn Abbas claimed that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah Zuhr and Asr together."
"2742","2737 - Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam, muzaffat, naqir, or dubba - Abu Dawud doubted."
"2743","2738 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take anything containing a soul as a target. I said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2744","2739 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Jabir informed me, from Ammar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like the nesting hollow of a sandgrouse for its eggs, Allah, mighty and majestic is He, builds for him a house in Paradise."
"2745","2740 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: Had you seen me while I was taking from the mud of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that mercy would reach him."
"2746","2741 - Abu Dawud said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about killing snakes. He said: Man and the snake were created alike: if he sees it, it frightens him, and if it bites him, it pains him; so kill them wherever you find them."
"2747","2742 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Iyas informed me, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: I came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, so I stood on his left; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed me on his right."
"2748","2743 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, that a woman vowed to perform Hajj, then died. Her brother asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What do you think, had she owed a debt, would you pay it? He said: Yes. He said: Then fulfill Allah's due, for He is most deserving of fulfillment."
"2749","2744 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, he said: My aunt Umm Hufayd gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, dried cheese and lizards. He ate of the clarified butter and dried cheese, and left the lizards out of aversion; they were eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and had they been forbidden they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2750","2745 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Hushaym narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man was thrown by his mount and died while in ihram. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in two garments with his head uncovered, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah."
"2751","2746 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"2752","2747 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and found the Jews fasting. He said: What is this? They said: This is a day on which Allah, mighty and majestic is He, drowned Pharaoh and saved Musa, peace be upon him, therein. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then I have more right to Musa. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting it."
"2753","2748 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast until they would say: He does not intend to break fast; and break fast until they would say: He does not intend to fast. And he did not fast a complete month since the day he came to Madinah except Ramadan."
"2754","2749 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ma'iz ibn Malik: Is what has reached me concerning you true? He said: What has reached you concerning me? He said: It has reached me that you committed adultery with the slave girl of the sons of So-and-so. He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned him away four times, then ordered him stoned."
"2755","2750 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi A'ishah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, mighty and majestic is He: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it}, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to endure hardship from the revelation, so he would move his lips - Ibn Abbas said: I only move my lips as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to move them. And Sa'id said: I only move my lips as I saw Ibn Abbas moving his lips - so Allah, blessed and exalted is He, revealed: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation}. He said: Gathering it in your heart, then you recite it. {So when We recite it, follow its recitation}, saying: Listen and be silent. {Then upon Us is its clarification}. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) thereafter, when Jibril, peace be upon him, departed, recited it as he had taught him."
"2756","2751 - Abu Dawud said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Dhuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha. I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended that his Ummah not be put to hardship."
"2757","2752 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Muslim al-Batin narrating from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned to him that her sister had vowed to fast a month, and that she had boarded a ship and died without fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Fast on behalf of your sister."
"2758","2753 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Muslim al-Batin narrating from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No deeds done on any days are better than those done on the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah. They said: O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad in the cause of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the cause of Allah, except a man who goes out with his life and his wealth in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and then returns with nothing of that."
"2759","2754 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he spent the night at the house of his maternal aunt Maymunah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came after the last Isha prayer and prayed four rak'ahs, then slept. Then he stood up and said: Has the boy slept? or some words like that. Then he stood to pray, so I stood to his left, and he took me and placed me to his right. Then he prayed five rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring, then he went out and prayed."
"2760","2755 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Sa'b ibn Jaththamah gave the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at Qudayd and in the state of ihram, the hind part of a wild donkey, dripping with blood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it."
"2761","2756 - Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and: Has there come upon man."
"2762","2757 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said regarding one who declares his wife unlawful to himself: It is an oath requiring expiation, and he said: You have indeed in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example."
"2763","2758 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Muslim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday the Surah of al-Jumu'ah and the Hypocrites, and he used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and: Has there come upon man."
"2764","2759 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed on the day of Eid two rak'ahs, praying neither before them nor after them. Then he went to the women, accompanied by Bilal, and urged them to give charity, so the women began to throw their earrings and their necklaces."
"2765","2760 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri and I went to al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu'man, and he dictated to Sufyan while I was with him, then when he stood up I copied it from Sufyan. So he narrated to us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us delivering an admonition and said: O people, you will be gathered to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised: As We began the first creation, We will repeat it, to the end of the verse. And the first of creation to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection will be Ibrahim (peace be upon him). And men from my Ummah will be brought and seized to the left, so I will say: My companions! Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. So I will say as the righteous servant said: And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them, to the end of the verse. Then it will be said to me: These have continued turning back on their heels since you left them."
"2766","2761 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when I was ten years old, circumcised, and I had already recited the Muhkam of the Qur'an. Shu'bah said: I said to Abu Bishr: What is the Muhkam of the Qur'an? He said: The Mufassal."
"2767","2762 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when I was fifteen years old and circumcised."
"2768","2763 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I was granted victory by the easterly wind, and Ad were destroyed by the westerly wind."
"2769","2764 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: This is an Umrah that we have enjoyed, so whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should exit ihram completely, for Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"2770","2765 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims. Then he said: If a drop of Zaqqum were to fall into the oceans of the world, it would corrupt the livelihoods of the people of the world, so how about one whose food it will be?"
"2771","2766 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in Ramadan, and when he reached Usfan he broke his fast."
"2772","2767 - Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid or Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been forbidden to pray behind sleepers and those engaged in conversation."
"2773","2768 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves and said: They are being punished for what is not grave in their view: as for one of them, he used to eat the flesh of people, and as for the other, he was a carrier of tales. Then he called for a palm stalk, split it into two halves, placed half on this grave and half on this grave, and said: Perhaps it will be lightened for them as long as they remain moist."
"2774","2769 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: One who prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me that he came upon a cast-aside grave, arranged them behind him, and prayed over it. So I said to al-Sha'bi: Who informed you, O Abu Amr? He said: Ibn Abbas informed me of it."
"2775","2770 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Zamzam and asked for water to drink, so I brought water, and he drank while standing."
"2776","2771 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: One who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit."
"2777","2772 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that he heard Abu al-Aliyah saying: The cousin of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning Ibn Abbas, narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a servant to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta, and he traced his lineage to his father."
"2778","2773 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say at times of distress: There is no god but Allah, the Magnificent, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Magnificent Throne; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens, Lord of the earths, and Lord of the Noble Throne."
"2779","2774 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the middle of his head, and he called it al-Munqidh."
"2780","2775 - Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah when it stood upon six pillars, and he stood at each pillar supplicating, and did not pray."
"2781","2776 - Abu Dawud said: Talhah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We, the company of the Prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, to delay our pre-dawn meal, and to place our right hands over our left hands in prayer."
"2782","2777 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, he said: I heard Ata saying: I bear witness regarding Ibn Abbas that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on the day of Eid, prayed, then delivered the sermon, then went to the women and urged them to give charity, so they began to throw their jewelry."
"2783","2778 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in the state of ihram."
"2784","2779 - Abu Dawud said: Rabbah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while he was fasting."
"2785","2780 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Isl ibn Sufyan al-Tamimi, from Ata, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer and gave the salutation after two rak'ahs of Maghrib, then he touched the Corner. When he was spoken to about that, he returned, bowed another rak'ah, and prostrated twice. Ibn Abbas was told of what Ibn al-Zubayr had done, so he said: He did not deviate from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2786","2781 - Abu Dawud said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibn Abbas; and Talhah, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been forbidden from nakedness, and that was before prophethood descended upon him."
"2787","2782 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Shall I not perform for you the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? We said: Yes indeed. So he performed ablution washing once each time: he rinsed his mouth once, sniffed water once, washed his face once, washed his hands up to the elbows once each, wiped his head, and washed his feet, with sandals on them, once each."
"2788","2783 - Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Khalid al-Qarazi narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people in station? They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man secluded in a mountain pass, establishing prayer and giving zakat, keeping away from the evils of people. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the worst of people in station? They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. He said: A man who is asked in the name of Allah and does not give."
"2789","2784 - Abu Dawud said: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a bone, or meat, then stand for prayer without performing ablution and without rinsing his mouth."
"2790","2785 - Yunus narrated to us; Abu Dawud said: al-Majishun and Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the Farewell and said: The obligation of Allah upon His servants regarding Hajj has met my father as a weak old man who cannot hold himself on a mount; will it suffice for him if I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"2791","2786 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, praying two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."
"2792","2787 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abu Taybah in the evening, and he cupped him and gave him his wage."
"2793","2788 - Abu Dawud said: Abbad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best times for you to be cupped are the seventeenth, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first."
"2794","2789 - Abu Dawud said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When this verse was revealed: And those who accuse chaste women and then do not bring four witnesses, to the end of the verse, Sa'd ibn Ubadah said: Was it revealed like this? If I were to find a wicked woman with a man over her, I would have no right to move him or disturb him until I bring four witnesses? By Allah, I will not bring four witnesses until he has finished his need. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the Ansar, do you not hear what your chief says? They said: O Messenger of Allah, do not blame him, for he is a jealous man; by Allah, he never married among us except a virgin, nor divorced a wife of his without any man among us daring to marry her, due to the intensity of his jealousy. So Sa'd said: By Allah, I know, O Messenger of Allah, that it is the truth and that it is from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, but I was surprised. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was like that, Hilal ibn Umayyah al-Waqifi came, one of the three to whom Allah turned in forgiveness, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came last night at evening time from a garden of mine where I had been, and I saw a man with my wife; I saw with my own eyes and heard with my own ears. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked what he brought, and it was said: Will Hilal be flogged and his testimony among the Muslims rendered void? So Hilal said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I see in your face that you dislike what I have brought, but I hope Allah will make a way out. He said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was like that, revelation descended upon him; and when revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his body and face would change for that, and his Companions would hold back from him and none of them would speak to him. When the revelation was lifted, he said: Rejoice, O Hilal. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call her. So she was called, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, knows that one of you is lying, so is either of you repentant? Hilal said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I have said nothing but the truth, and I have spoken the truth. He said: At that she said: He has lied. He said: It was said to Hilal: Will you testify four testimonies by Allah that you are among the truthful? And at the fifth it was said to him: O Hilal, fear Allah, for the punishment of Allah is severer than the punishment of people, and this is the decisive one that makes the punishment due upon you. He said: By Allah, Allah will never punish me for it, just as He did not have me flogged for it. So he testified the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he were among the liars. And it was said to her: Testify four testimonies by Allah that he is among the liars, and at the fifth it was said to her: O woman, fear Allah, for the punishment of Allah is severer than the punishment of people, and this is the decisive one that makes the punishment due upon you. She hesitated for a while, then said: By Allah, I will not disgrace my people, so she testified the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he were among the truthful. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed that neither she nor her child be accused, and whoever accuses her or her child will be flogged with the prescribed punishment; and she has no maintenance nor lodging due from him, because they separate without divorce and without his having died leaving her a widow. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch her; if she bears him thick-haired, fair, bow-legged, thin-shanked, then he is the son of Hilal ibn Umayyah, and if she bears him thick-shanked, full-buttocked, dark, curly-haired, camel-like, then he belongs to her companion. He said: She bore him dark, curly-haired, camel-like, thick-shanked, full-buttocked. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the oaths, there would have been between me and her a matter. Abbad said: I heard Ikrimah saying: I saw him as a governor of one of the garrison towns, with his father unknown."
"2795","2790 - Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was shown in my dream in Ramadan while I was sleeping, and it was said to me: Tonight is the Night of Decree. So I woke up, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying. I took hold of the tent rope, and it was the night of the twenty-fourth. I looked at the sun in its morning, and it had no rays."
"2796","2791 - Abu Dawud said: Sharik and Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year? He said: No, rather one Hajj; had I said every year, it would have been every year."
"2797","2792 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and spoke eloquent speech, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and indeed, some poetry is wisdom."
"2798","2793 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast Ramadan upon seeing it, and break the fast upon seeing it; if a cloud or haze comes between you and it, complete the month of Sha'ban as thirty, and do not anticipate Ramadan by fasting a day of Sha'ban."
"2799","2794 - Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a small mat."
"2800","2795 - Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, turned His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward the Ka'bah and prayer toward it, they said: What about those of our companions who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And Allah would never let your faith go to waste."
"2801","2796 - Abu Dawud said: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the paternal aunt of Abdullah ibn al-Harith accepted Islam, emigrated, and married, while her husband had accepted Islam before her, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her to her husband."
"2802","2797 - Abu Dawud said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledged allegiance with a man, and when he had pledged him he said: Choose. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Such is the sale."
"2803","2798 - Abu Dawud said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood among his Companions, and some of them inherited from others, until there was revealed: And blood relatives are more entitled to one another. So they abandoned that and inherited by kinship."
"2804","2799 - Abu Dawud said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast while traveling and break his fast."
"2805","2800 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Ikrimah narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: Fair-skinned, of noble bearing, one-eyed, the most resembling of people to Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan, or he said: Qatr. If the doomed perish in doubt, then your Lord is not one-eyed."
"2806","2801 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed men who imitate women and women who imitate men."
"2807","2802 - Abu Dawud said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the Night of Decree: A smooth, bright night, neither hot nor cold; its sun rises in its morning weak and red."
"2808","2803 - Abu Dawud said: Abbad narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is antimony, for it clears the sight and grows the hair. And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a kohl container from which he would apply kohl every night, three times in this eye and three times in this eye."
"2809","2804 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not boast of your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic ignorance, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, what the dung beetle rolls with its nose is better than your forefathers who died in the pre-Islamic ignorance."
"2810","2805 - Abu Dawud said: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Sawdah feared that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would divorce her, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, do not divorce me; keep me, and make my day for Aishah. So he did, and this verse was revealed: And if a woman fears from her husband discord or turning away, to the end of the verse. He said: Whatever they agree upon of anything is permissible."
"2811","2806 - Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I used to hear the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the house while I was in the room."
"2812","2806M - Abu Dawud said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not withhold milk in the udder, and let none of you outbid another to inflate prices."
"2813","2807 - Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Conquest of Makkah took place, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw cheese and said: What is this? They said: This is a food made in the land of the non-Arabs. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put the knife in it, mention the name of Allah, and eat."
"2814","2808 - Abu Dawud said: Habib ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Harim, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr to make a stipulation in Hajj, and she did that by the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2815","2809 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blood money for a contractually freed slave is paid in proportion to what has been freed of him as that of a free man, and in proportion to what remains enslaved of him as that of a slave. He said: And Ali and Marwan used to say that."
"2816","2810 - Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge from the east people who recite the Qur'an without it passing beyond their throats; they will shoot out of the religion, or he said: out of Islam, as the arrow shoots out of the target."
"2817","2811 - Abu Dawud said: al-Harith Abu Qudamah narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq or a man, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not prostrate in any of the Mufassal after he moved to Madinah."
"2818","2812 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: If they were brought to me I would kill them, due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever changes his religion, kill him."
"2819","2813 - Abu Dawud said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Malik - Abu Dawud said: I think he is Ibn Abi Bashir - from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take good omens and would not take bad omens, and the good name would please him."
"2820","2814 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us with Usamah riding behind him, so we gave him to drink of this nabidh, meaning the nabidh of the waterskin."
"2821","2815 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the saying of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: When you contract a debt for a specified term, write it down, to the end of the verse: The first one to deny was Adam. Allah showed him his offspring, and he saw a radiant man whose light shone. He said: O Lord, who is this? He said: This is your son Dawud. He said: O Lord, what is his lifespan? He said: Sixty years. He said: O Lord, add to his lifespan. He said: No, unless you add to him from your own lifespan. He said: And what is my lifespan? He said: A thousand years. Adam said: I have granted him forty years. He said: So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, wrote a document against him and had His angels bear witness over him. When death came to him and the angels came to him, he said: There remain forty years of my life. They said: You granted them to your son Dawud. He said: I granted nothing to anyone. He said: So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, brought out the document, and His angels bore witness against him."
"2822","2816 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril said to me: O Muhammad, had you seen me while I was taking mud of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that mercy would reach him."
"2823","2817 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When Uthman ibn Maz'un passed away, his wife said: Congratulations to you, O son of Maz'un, Paradise. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at her with the look of an angry man. She said: O Messenger of Allah, your horseman and your companion! He said: I do not know what will be done with him. That weighed heavily upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was counted among their best, until Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), passed away. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join our righteous predecessor Uthman ibn Maz'un. He said: And the women wept over Ruqayyah, so Umar began to forbid them or strike them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Umar. He said: Then he said: Beware the croaking of Satan; for whatever comes from the eye and the heart is from mercy, and whatever comes from the tongue and the hand is from Satan. He said: And Fatimah, may Allah have mercy on her, wept at the edge of Ruqayyah's grave, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began wiping the tears from her face with his hand, or he said: with his garment."
"2824","2818 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that he heard Abu Hassan al-A'raj narrating from Sulaym ibn Abd al-Hujaymi, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: What are these reports that have spread among the people, saying: Whoever circumambulates the House has exited ihram? He said: That is the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), even if you dislike it."
"2825","2819 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan al-A'raj, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, he marked his sacrificial camel on the right side of its hump. Shu'bah said: Then he wiped the blood from it. And Hisham said: Then he removed the blood from it, and he entered ihram for Hajj. Hisham said: And he entered ihram at noon, and he garlanded it with two sandals. Shu'bah said: I narrated this hadith to Sufyan al-Thawri, and he said: Was there in the world one like Qatadah, meaning in hadith."
"2826","2820 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Asim al-Ghanawi, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House upon a camel, and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truly and falsely. I said: How truly and falsely? He said: They spoke truly: he circumambulated upon a camel, but it is not Sunnah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was such that people were not struck away from him nor pushed back, so he circumambulated upon a camel so they could hear his speech and their hands could not reach him. I said: They claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran around the House, and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truly and falsely. I said: How truly and falsely? He said: They spoke truly: he did run, but they lied: it is not Sunnah; Quraysh said: Leave Muhammad and his Companions until they die the death of the naghaf worm. Then when they made peace with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they would come the following year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions arrived, with the idolaters on the side of Qu'ayqi'an, and he said to his Companions: Run briskly, but it is not Sunnah. I said: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is Sunnah. He said: They spoke truly: when the rites were shown to Ibrahim (peace be upon him), Satan appeared to him at the place of running, so he raced him and Ibrahim outran him. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) took him on until he brought him to Mina and said: This is the camping place of the people. Then he reached the Jamrah of al-Aqabah, and Satan appeared to him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he went away with him to the middle Jamrah; Satan appeared to him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then he came to the farthest Jamrah, and Satan appeared to him, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he went away. Then he brought him to Muzdalifah and said: This is the Sacred Monument. Then he brought him to Arafah and said: This is Arafah. Ibn Abbas said: Do you know why it was named Arafah? He said: No. He said: Because Jibril said to him: Have you recognized? Ibn Abbas said: Do you know how the Talbiyah came about? He said: When Ibrahim was commanded to proclaim Hajj among the people, the mountains were commanded and lowered their heads, and the villages were raised for him, and he proclaimed Hajj among the people."
"2827","2821 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting."
"2828","2822 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched Ja'far, Zayd, and Ibn Rawahah, meaning in the army of Mu'tah. Ibn Rawahah stayed behind while the people went on, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What kept you behind? He said: O Messenger of Allah, Friday prayers, which I will attend, then I will go. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning march in the cause of Allah, or an evening march, is better than the world and all it contains."
"2829","2823 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while fasting and in ihram."
"2830","2824 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted in Ramadan, and when he reached Usfan he broke his fast."
"2831","2825 - Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Arafat and the people urged their mounts on, it was announced among the people: O people, piety is not in urging on horses and camels. I never saw a hand lifted in haste until he reached Muzdalifah."
"2832","2826 - Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the weak of his family on the night of Muzdalifah, and he came upon a young boy among them, moved him with his foot, and said: Do not stone the Jamrah of al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
"2833","2827 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Dharr, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Ibn Abbas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us finds something speaking to himself, such that becoming charred remains is dearer to him than speaking of it? One of the two narrators said: He said: Praise be to Allah, Who could do nothing against you except whispering. And the other said: Praise be to Allah, Who reduced his affair to whispering."
"2834","2828 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of them, or if one of you, when he comes to his wife, says: O Allah, keep me away from Satan, and keep Satan away from what You grant us, and a child is decreed between them, Satan will not harm him, or: Satan will not be given power over him. Al-A'mash did not raise it as marfu', while Mansur did."
"2835","2829 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Kurayb ibn Abi Muslim narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, and I watched the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He slept, then woke, washed his face and his hands, then slept. Then he woke, went to a waterskin, untied its binding, meaning its cord, then poured into a basin or bowl, washed his hands and face, and performed a good ablution between the two ablutions. Then he stood to pray, so I stood to his left, and he placed me to his right. The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) totaled thirteen rak'ahs. In his prostration, or he said: in his prayer - Shu'bah doubted - he used to say: O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my heart, light in my sight, light above me, light beneath me, light behind me, light before me, light to my right, light to my left, and make me light, or: make light for me - Shu'bah doubted. Then he slept until he snored, and we used to know his sleep by his snoring. Then he went out to prayer."
"2836","2830 - Abu Dawud said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uqbah informed me, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a boy of hers: Is there Hajj for him? He said: And for you there is reward."
"2837","2831 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father began speaking to him while he turned away from him, facing a man. When we went out, he said to me: O my son, did you see your cousin? I was speaking to him and he would not answer me. I said: O father, did you not see the man who was with him speaking to him? He said: No. He said: Was there anyone with him? He said: Yes. He said: So he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, was there anyone with you? He said: And did you see him? He said: Abdullah informed me of that. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to me and said: Did you see him? I said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril (peace be upon him)."
"2838","2832 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that he recited this verse: Today I have perfected for you your religion, completed upon you My favor, and approved for you Islam as religion, while a Jewish man was with him. He said: Had this been revealed upon us, we would have taken its day as a festival. So Ibn Abbas said: It was indeed revealed on a Friday, the day of Arafah, or the evening of Arafah."
"2839","2833 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Bara ibn Yazid al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four things, saying: I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the trial of the one-eyed liar."
"2840","2834 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, who said: Ibn Abbas addressed us upon the pulpit of Basrah, praised Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and extolled Him, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Prophet but that he has a supplication; all of them have hastened it in this world, but I have stored my supplication as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection. And I am the chief of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting; the first over whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting; in my hand is the Banner of Praise, under it Adam and all below him, without boasting. The distress of that Day will weigh heavily upon people, so they will say: Come with us to Adam, the father of mankind, that he intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. So they will come to Adam (peace be upon him) and say: You are the one whom Allah created with His Hand, settled in His Paradise, and made His angels prostrate to you; intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. He will say: I am not in a position for that; I was expelled from Paradise due to my sin, and today nothing concerns me but myself. Rather, go to Nuh, the first of the Prophets. So they will come to Nuh (peace be upon him) and say: Intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. He will say: I am not in a position for that; I made a supplication that drowned the people of the earth, and today nothing concerns me but myself. Rather, go to Ibrahim, the intimate friend of Allah. So they will come to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and say: Intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. He will say: I am not in a position for that; I told three lies in the cause of Islam, and today nothing concerns me but myself - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, he intended by them nothing but the religion of Allah: his saying: Indeed I am sick, his saying: Rather, the chief of them did it, and his saying to Sarah: Say: He is my brother - rather, go to Musa, a servant whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech. So they will come to Musa and say: Intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. He will say: I am not in a position for that; I killed a soul without a soul in return, and today nothing concerns me but myself. Rather, go to Isa, the Spirit of Allah and His Word. So they will come to Isa and say: Intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. He will say: I am not in a position for that; I and my mother were taken as two gods besides Allah. But have you considered: if goods were in a vessel sealed over, would one reach what is in the vessel until the seal is broken? They will say: No. He will say: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has come today, and he has been forgiven what preceded of his sin and what followed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So the people will come to me and say: Intercede for us with our Lord until He judges between us. So I will say: I am for it, I am for it, until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, permits whomever He wills and is pleased with. When Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, intends to judge among His creation, a caller will call: Where is Ahmad and his Ummah? So I will stand, and my Ummah will follow me, radiant with traces of purification. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So we are the last and the first: the first to be reckoned, and the nations will make way for us from their path, and the nations will say: This Ummah almost all became Prophets. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I will reach the gate of Paradise and ask for it to be opened. It will be said: Who is this? I will say: Ahmad. So it will be opened for me. I will reach my Lord, Who is upon His Throne, and fall prostrate. I will praise my Lord with praises with which none before me praised Him, nor will anyone after me praise Him therewith. It will be said to me: Raise your head, speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. So I will intercede, and it will be said: Go and bring out of the Fire whoever had in his heart such-and-such of good. So I will go and bring them out. Then I will return to my Lord and fall prostrate. It will be said to me: Raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be accepted, ask and you will be given. He said: So a limit will be set for me, and I will bring them out."
"2841","2835 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to me, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A woman used to pray behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the most beautiful of people. He said: Some people would pray in the last rows of the men in order to look at her. He said: One of them would look at her from under his armpit, while another would advance to the first row so as not to see her. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: And We know those of you who go forward, and We know those who lag behind."
"2842","2836 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hantam, the dubba, the naqir, and the muzaffat."
"2843","2837 - Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have nabidh made for him in a waterskin, and he would drink from it that day, the second day up to the third day; if any remained he would pour it away."
"2844","2838 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah and Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have nabidh made for him in a waterskin, and he would drink it that day and the second day. Shu'bah said: Until the afternoon. And Abu Isra'il said: Until the third day; if any remained he would pour it away."
"2845","2839 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that a mouse fell into solidified clarified butter belonging to the family of Maymunah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the mouse and what was around it be taken."
"2846","2840 - Abu Dawud said: Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that Sa'd ibn Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding a vow incumbent upon his mother; she died without fulfilling it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"2847","2841 - Abu Dawud said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in Ramadan, and when he reached al-Kadid he broke his fast; and only the later and later of the actions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is to be taken."
"2848","2842 - Abu Dawud said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that he performed Hajj tamattu' with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2849","2843 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Shaqiq al-Uqayli narrated to us, who said: Ibn Abbas addressed us in Basrah, and continued addressing until the sun set and the stars appeared. A man of Banu Tamim clung calling: Prayer, prayer! So Ibn Abbas said to him: May you lose your mother! Are you teaching me the Sunnah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers, meaning Maghrib and Isha. Ibn Shaqiq said: Something of that remained in my soul until I met Abu Hurayrah and asked him, and he confirmed him."
"2850","2844 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari saying: We sighted the Ramadan crescent while at Dhat Irq, so we sent a man to Ibn Abbas to ask him. Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has extended it for its sighting; if it is obscured from you, complete the number."
"2851","2845 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari saying: I asked Ibn Abbas about advance payment for dates, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling dates until some are eaten of them, or eaten, or until weighed. A man said to Ibn Abbas: What is weighed? A man beside him said: Until estimated. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah used to be angry at this man, saying: Why did he not keep silent until Ibn Abbas spoke."
"2852","2846 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and others narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd - Shu'bah said: from Umar ibn Harmalah, and others said: Ibn Harmalah - from Ibn Abbas, who said: My maternal aunt gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarified butter, lizards, and milk; with him were Khalid ibn al-Walid to his left and I to his right. He spat upon it, meaning upon the lizards, or a similar word. Khalid said to him: As if you found it distasteful? He said: Yes, or he said: Indeed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank of the milk and said: The drink is yours, and if you wish you may give it to Khalid, or he said: your uncle, or: your cousin, meaning Khalid. I said: I would not prefer anyone with your leftover. He said: So he handed it to me and I drank, then I gave Khalid to drink. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know of no drink that suffices in place of food except milk; when one of you drinks it, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and increase us of it. And whoever among you eats food, meaning of that lizard, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and feed us better than it."
"2853","2847 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn Abbas, that Umm al-Fadl sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a vessel of milk while he was at Arafah on the day of Arafah, standing, and he drank."
"2854","2848 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Qariz, from Abu Ghatfan, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas perform ablution, rinsing his mouth and sniffing water twice, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rinses his mouth and blows his nose, let him do that twice thoroughly, or three times."
"2855","2849 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Abbas and I came upon a she-donkey, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying. We dismounted and passed in front of him, and he neither turned us back nor forbade us."
"2856","2850 - Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Your freedman, when he prostrates, draws his hands to his sides. Ibn Abbas said: That is the crouching of a dog. I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"2857","2851 - Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, who said: When Ibn Abbas bathed from major impurity, he would pour with his right over his left seven times. He said: One day he began pouring over his left, and said to me: Do you know how much I poured? I said: No. He said: May you lose your mother, why do you not know? So he poured over his left seven times, performed ablution as for prayer, then poured over his head, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that."
"2858","2852 - Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me among the weak of his family, and we stoned the Jamrah at dawn."
"2859","2853 - Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, who said: al-Miswar ibn Makhramah entered upon Ibn Abbas while he was ill, wearing a garment of brocade, with before him a brazier bearing images. Al-Miswar said: What is this, O Ibn Abbas? Ibn Abbas said: I did not know of it; and I do not consider the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to have forbidden this except due to arrogance and tyranny, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that. When al-Miswar left, Ibn Abbas ordered the garment removed from him, and said: Cut off the heads of these images."
"2860","2854 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: Ibn Abbas narrated to me, who said: A group of Jews came one day to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us of matters we ask you about, known only to a Prophet. He said: Ask me whatever you wish, but grant me the covenant of Allah and what Ya'qub took from his sons: if I tell you something you recognize, you will pledge to me upon Islam. They said: That is yours. He said: So ask me whatever you wish. They said: Inform us of four matters we ask you about: inform us of the food that Isra'il forbade himself before the Torah was revealed; inform us of the water of the woman in relation to the water of the man, and how the male comes from it to be male, and how the female comes from it to be female; inform us how this Prophet is in sleep, and who is your patron among the angels? He said: Upon you is the covenant of Allah and His pledge: if I tell you, will you pledge to me? So they gave him whatever covenant and pledge he wished. He said: I adjure you by Allah Who revealed the Torah upon Musa: do you know that Isra'il, Ya'qub, fell severely ill with a prolonged sickness, and vowed to Allah a vow: if He cured him of his sickness, he would forbid himself his most beloved drink and his most beloved food; and his most beloved drink was camel milk, and his most beloved food was camel meat? They said: O Allah, yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bear witness over them. He said: So I adjure you by Allah, besides Whom there is no god, Who revealed the Torah upon Musa: do you know that the water of the man is thick and white, and the water of the woman is thin and yellow; whichever prevails, the child and resemblance belong to it by Allah's permission: if the water of the man prevails over the water of the woman, it is male by Allah's permission, and if the water of the woman prevails over the water of the man, it is female by Allah's permission? They said: O Allah, yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bear witness. He said: So I adjure you by Allah Who revealed the Torah upon Musa: do you know that the eyes of this Prophet sleep while his heart does not sleep? They said: O Allah, yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness over them. They said: Now you: tell us who is your patron among the angels; upon that we will join you or part from you. He said: My patron is Jibril, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, never sent a Prophet but that he was his patron. They said: Upon that we part from you; had your patron been other than him among the angels, we would have pledged to you and believed you. He said: What prevents you from believing him? They said: He is our enemy among the angels. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril, for he brought it down upon your heart by Allah's permission, to the end of the verse; and there was revealed: So they drew upon themselves anger upon anger."
"2861","2855 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman should travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her except with a mahram present. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife intends to perform Hajj, while I intend to go out in such-and-such an army. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj with your wife."
"2862","2856 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, he said: I heard Abu Salih, who had grown old, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed women who frequently visit graves, and those who take them as places of worship and lamps."
"2863","2857 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Fadl rode behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Arafah, and began glancing at a woman. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O boy, for this is a day in which whoever guards his sight will be forgiven."
"2864","2858 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah have mercy on them both, narrated that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon the wood of his pulpit: People will either cease neglecting the Friday prayers, or Allah will seal their hearts, and they will surely be recorded among the heedless."
"2865","2859 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I was praying, and the caller to prayer began the iqamah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled me and said: Do you pray Fajr as four?"
"2866","2860 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu al-Safar narrating from Sa'id ibn Shufi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his house traveling, he would pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, until he returned."
"2867","2861 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man freed a slave of his, then died leaving no heir besides him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made him inherit from him; he made the lower inherit from the higher."
"2868","2862 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Tamimi, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the toothstick, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept commanding us with it until we feared something would be revealed to him concerning it."
"2869","2863 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Tamimi narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"2870","2864 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf narrated to me, who said: I prayed behind Ibn Abbas over a funeral while I was then a young man, and I heard him reciting the Opening of the Book over it. When I had prayed, I came and took his hand and said: O Abu al-Abbas, what is this? He said: This is right and Sunnah, or he said: Sunnah and right."
"2871","2865 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: When I cannot catch the prayer in the Sacred Mosque, how much should I pray at al-Batha? He said: Two rak'ahs; that is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2872","2866 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept away from his wives for a month. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Muhammad, the month is complete; the month is twenty-nine."
"2873","2867 - And with it: I asked Ibn Abbas about nabidh, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earthen jar and the gourd. And Ibn Abbas said: Whoever holds unlawful what Allah and His Messenger have made unlawful should hold nabidh unlawful."
"2874","2868 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Abu Bishr, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast with fangs and every bird with talons."
"2875","2869 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hushaym and Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah al-Qassab, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Mu'awiyah to write for him. He said: He is eating. Then he sent for him and he said: He is eating. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah not fill his belly. Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Faris, the narrator from Yunus ibn Habib, said: Its meaning, and Allah knows best: May Allah not fill his belly in this world, so that he not be among those who hunger on the Day of Resurrection; because the report from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that he said: The longest of people in satiety in this world will be the longest of them in hunger on the Day of Resurrection."
"2876","2870 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: When the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Who are the people? They said: From Rabi'ah. He said: Welcome to the delegation, neither disgraced nor regretful. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a tribe of Rabi'ah, we come to you from a distant land, and between us and you stands this tribe of the disbelievers of Mudar, and we can reach you only in a sacred month. So command us with a decisive matter that we may call to it those behind us and enter Paradise through it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I command you with four and forbid you four: I command you with faith in Allah alone. Do you know what faith in Allah is? Testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting Ramadan, and giving the fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you four: the gourd, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat. And perhaps he said: the muqayyar. So memorize them and call to them those behind you."
"2877","2871 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray thirteen rak'ahs at night."
"2878","2872 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, who said: I performed tamattu', meaning in Hajj, and asked Ibn Abbas, and he commanded me with it. When I slept, I saw in my dream as if a speaker was saying: An accepted Hajj and an accepted Umrah. So I came to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: The Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Then he said: Stay with me, and I will allot you a share of my wealth. He said: So I stayed, and I used to interpret between him and the people, and he would seat me with him upon the couch."
"2879","2873 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2880","2874 - Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jamrah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Makkah thirteen years receiving revelation, and in Madinah ten, and he died at sixty-three years of age."
"2881","2875 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are the guardian of every believer after me."
"2882","2876 - And with it, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The first to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after Khadijah was Ali."
"2883","2877 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, he said: I heard Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and a kid goat began trying to pass in front of him, so he kept warding it off from passing in front of him."
"2884","2878 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam and Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from a man of Banu Tamim, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of wine are unlawful."
"2885","2879 - Abu Dawud said: Abu Talhah the blind narrated to us, from a man he named, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O youths of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; for whoever has his youth kept sound by Allah will enter Paradise."
"2886","2880 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, and a man came to him and said: Who are you? He said: So he claimed kinship with him through a distant tie, and he softened his speech to him. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn your lineages so that you may join your ties of kinship; for there is no closeness through kinship when it is severed, even if near, and no distance through it when it is joined, even if distant."
"2887","2881 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me ahead among the baggage of his family from Muzdalifah by night."
"2888","2882 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim, Salm ibn Zarir, Hammad ibn Najih, and Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into Paradise and most of its people were the poor; and I looked into the Fire and most of its people were women."
"2889","2883 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Muttalib, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution washing once each time."
"2890","2884 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah and Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We raid toward the east and are brought waterskins of which we do not know what they are. He said: I do not know what you say, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every hide that is tanned has become pure."
"2891","2885 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Suhayb - I said: Who is Suhayb? He said: A man of Basrah - from Ibn Abbas, that he was upon a donkey, he and a boy of Banu Hashim, and passed in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and he did not turn away for that. And two young girls of Banu Abd al-Muttalib came and took hold of the knees of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he separated between them, meaning he parted them, and did not turn away for that."
"2892","2886 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj; those of his Companions who had no sacrificial animal with them exited ihram, while those with sacrificial animals did not exit ihram. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Talhah were among those who had sacrificial animals with them."
"2893","2887 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the witr, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: One rak'ah at the end of the night."
"2894","2888 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the privy, and they said: Shall we bring you water for ablution? He said: Am I to pray, that I should perform ablution?!"
"2895","2889 - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr, who said: One who heard Ibn Abbas informed us, narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he urinated, then took to eating. It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you have urinated. He said: Do I intend to pray?!"
"2896","2890 - Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us ahead, the young boys of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, upon donkeys from Muzdalifah, tapping our thighs and saying: My little sons, do not stone the Jamrah of al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
